# ── Chapter 12 fidelity pins: "A Place in Which Life Remains Possible" ──────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/12-a-place-in-which-life-remains-possible.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # all substantive pins and contradiction checks
#
# The chapter's case lists tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/fixture.nibli.
# Its worked water and river example also supplies
# tests/pins/ecology/scarcity/water-animal-conflict-is-not-use-permission/fixture.nibli.
#
# The ecological and animal family's own cases carry the environmental claim,
# the axes, the Guardian route, the authorisations and the withdrawals —
# tests/pins/ecology/. The liberty-environment pins carry the Class Nine
# barriers:
#   book-1/source/liberty-environment.pins.nibli     FS-CCE-09, 10, 21..33
#
# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE: a FALSE is pinned only where the KB could have said
# TRUE, and the comment says what would flip it.

:expect-pins 38

# "The environmental right stands beside the floor rather than becoming one of
# its items": the floor's inventory refuses it as a further item, and the
# floor gives no ground for erasing an ecological ceiling.
? prevents(MaterialFloorInventory, EnvironmentalNinthFloor).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MaterialFloor, EcologicalCeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

# Each person also holds a barrier against ecology "selecting floor loss" for
# them; the rules conclude it for Adam from personhood alone.
? prevents(Adam, EcologySelectedFloorLoss).
# => TRUE

# "Each condition is judged on its own: a failure on one axis stays a failure
# whatever is gained on another" — axis by axis.
? prevents(ClimateAtmosphere, CeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

? prevents(CleanAir, CeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

? prevents(WatersAndWetlands, CeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

? prevents(LivingSoil, CeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

? prevents(BiodiversityAndHabitats, CeilingErasure).
# => TRUE

# "the protected object is the ecological capability and the reasonable
# options inherited by whoever later exists", and it may not be exhausted.
? prevents(FutureEcologicalCapability, CommonsExhaustion).
# => TRUE

# "Scientific assessment, law-making, advocacy and adjudication remain
# separate functions", and "Uncertainty is not safety."
? prevents(EcologicalCeiling, ScienceLawFunctionFusion).
# => TRUE

? prevents(EcologicalCeiling, UncertaintyTreatedAsSafety).
# => TRUE

# "No offset excuses a ceiling breach"
? prevents(EcologicalBreach, OffsetExcuse).
# => TRUE

# "Urgent public repair stays owed when the responsible actor is unknown,
# absent or insolvent."
? prevents(RestorationDuty, InsolvencyDelay).
# => TRUE

# The person-held environmental barriers, for a cast member by name.
? prevents(Adam, EnvironmentalConditionsDenial).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, EnvironmentalInformationWithholding).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, UnassessedHighConsequenceDecision).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, UnreasonedEnvironmentalDecision).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, EnvironmentalPublicPrivateEvasion).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, EnvironmentalWorthRanking).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Adam, EcologicalReviewDenial).
# => TRUE

# The child with nobody, on the one-line birth record: "Every person has an
# independently enforceable environmental right", and Nell holds these
# barriers as Adam does.
? prevents(Nell, EnvironmentalConditionsDenial).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, EnvironmentalInformationWithholding).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, EnvironmentalWorthRanking).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, EcologicalReviewDenial).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, EcologySelectedFloorLoss).
# => TRUE

# "The environmental right stands beside the floor": the State's care debt to
# Nell holds too, concluded from personhood alone.
? owe(State, Healthy, Nell).
# => TRUE

# Essential water and a river limit. The animal claim in the same river is
# the next chapter's.
# The paired positive supplies the actual economic allocation:
# tests/pins/ecology/scarcity/water-separate-physical-allocation/expect.pins.nibli
# The complete continuity record obliges its named responsible actor to
# preserve the immediate floor, obtain alternatives and repair the breach, and
# bars calling the unmet floor a success or the breached limit compliance.
? complete(RiverWaterContinuityRecord, ECDualFloorAndCeilingContinuity, ExistingEssentialWaterService).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RiverWaterV14, ECPreserveImmediateFloorWhileObtainingAlternativesAndRepairingBreach, RiverWaterContinuityRecord).
# => TRUE
? prevents(RiverWaterContinuityRecord, ECUnmetFloorRenamedSuccess).
# => TRUE
? prevents(RiverWaterContinuityRecord, ECCeilingBreachRenamedCompliance).
# => TRUE
# "Dividing water among people is a separate decision": with no scarcity
# comparison recorded, the rules conclude neither an allocation permission
# nor an allocation duty for FSBOD_09.
? permits(FSBOD_09, ECOnlyExistingRightsPreservingPhysicalScarcityAllocation, RiverWaterAllocationRecord).
# => FALSE
? obliged(FSBOD_09, ECPreserveActualScarcitySafeguardsFloorContinuityAndSeparateEcologicalFailure, RiverWaterAllocationRecord).
# => FALSE
# The claimant: "the claimant remains a person owed care and keeps the vote".
# No receipt shows care received, and the rules conclude no confinement and
# no credibility finding.
? person(RiverWaterClaimant).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Healthy, RiverWaterClaimant).
# => TRUE
? decide(RiverWaterClaimant, Ballot).
# => TRUE
? healthy(RiverWaterClaimant).
# => FALSE
? false(RiverWaterClaimant).
# => FALSE
? prisoner(RiverWaterClaimant).
# => FALSE
